Package: zukzeit
Title: Native Time-Series Foundation Models
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Pedro", "Botz", , "pedrobtz@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre", "cph")),
    person("Google", "LLC", role = c("cph", "ctb"),
           comment = "TimesFM reference implementation"),
    person("Datadog", "Inc.", role = c("cph", "ctb"),
           comment = "Toto reference implementation"),
    person("Amazon.com", "Inc.", role = c("cph", "ctb"),
           comment = "Chronos-2 reference implementation")
    )
Description: Runs open time-series foundation models natively in 'R'. It
    provides a pretrained-checkpoint loader backed by a curated catalogue and an
    architecture constructor registry, a
    versioned execution contract and conformance harness, explicit capability
    metadata, batched panel inference with device resolution, and a standard
    forecast object backed by 'distributional'. The supported native
    architectures are 'TimesFM' 2.5, 'Toto' 2.0, and 'Chronos-2', each loaded
    from an immutable checkpoint and verified against pinned reference outputs;
    see Das et al. (2024) <doi:10.48550/arXiv.2310.10688>, Khwaja et al. (2026)
    <doi:10.48550/arXiv.2605.20119>, and Ansari et al. (2025)
    <doi:10.48550/arXiv.2510.15821>. The engine is framework-neutral, with
    optional adapters for 'tidymodels' (via 'parsnip' and 'dials') and the
    'tidyverts' ecosystem (via 'fabletools').
